        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "Durable Core PR 5/6: add operation-scoped execution recovery",
        "body": "## Stack Position\n\nDurable Core PR 5/6, submitted only after the latest completed ClawSweeper\nverdict for PR4 #111343 reached at least Gold Shrimp.\n\nThis PR targets `release/2026.7.1`, so GitHub shows the cumulative durable-core\nstack. The reviewable PR5-only delta is:\n\nhttps://github.com/mjnkao/openclaw/compare/codex/durable-core-pr4-agent-turn-v1...codex/durable-core-pr5-execution-worker-v1\n\n- Stack parent: `456ca1b7e0118acc69c9bdaf68d88526cbf5234c`\n- Exact head: `2c69a09edeb0860d7885d23ac345bab770ee6bab`\n- PR5-only delta: 15 files, 3,552 additions, 12 deletions\n- Database schema delta from PR4: none\n- Configuration delta from PR4: none\n- Public Gateway or CLI mutation surface: none\n\n## What Problem This Solves\n\nPR2 persisted generic execution records, and PR3-PR4 added owner recovery and\ndurable front-door admission. Those pieces still need a narrowly scoped way to\nexecute explicitly registered durable operations and classify expired claims\nafter a process disappears.\n\nThis slice adds an exact `operationKind@operationVersion` registry, executor,\nworker, and expired-claim recovery path. It does not turn the Gateway into a\ngeneric workflow engine and it does not claim that arbitrary agent turns or\ntool processes can be replayed.\n\n## Contract\n\n- A worker may claim only an exact registered operation kind and version.\n- Stable worker identity and per-attempt claim tokens are separate; heartbeat\n  and settlement writes are fenced by the claim token.\n- Start, heartbeat, refs, settlement, timers, uncertainty, wakes, and terminal\n  evidence use caller-composed SQLite transactions.\n- Infrastructure persistence failures roll back the state bundle and remain\n  infrastructure failures.\n- Expired claims requeue automatically only for explicit no-side-effect,\n  idempotent, or idempotency-key-backed work.\n- Unsafe expired claims become `unknown_after_side_effect` and wake their\n  canonical owner without replay.\n- Missing handlers become `requires_owner_decision` and wake their owner;\n  they are not claimed by a generic fallback.\n- Existing agent-turn and chat-send owners are registered as definitions but\n  receive no generic replay handler.\n\n## Exact-Head Fault Proof\n\nAn isolated shared SQLite database and three independent connections modeled a\nprocess disappearing after a handler returned but before settlement committed.\n\nFor `proof.idempotent@1`, injected failure of\n`runtime.step.succeeded` rolled back the output and terminal event. A new\nconnection and registry recovered the expired claim, requeued it because its\nowner declared idempotency, and completed with one output ref and one terminal\nevent:\n\n```json\n{\n  \"handlerCalls\": 2,\n  \"recovery\": {\n    \"scanned\": 1,\n    \"requeued\": 1,\n    \"requiresOwnerDecision\": 0,\n    \"unknownAfterSideEffect\": 0,\n    \"raced\": 0\n  },\n  \"terminalEvents\": 1,\n  \"outputRefs\": 1\n}\n```\n\nFor `proof.unsafe@1`, the same settlement fault produced no replay:\n\n```json\n{\n  \"handlerCalls\": 1,\n  \"recovery\": {\n    \"scanned\": 1,\n    \"requeued\": 0,\n    \"requiresOwnerDecision\": 0,\n    \"unknownAfterSideEffect\": 1,\n    \"raced\": 0\n  },\n  \"replayClaimed\": false,\n  \"recoveryState\": \"unknown_after_side_effect\"\n}\n```\n\nAn expired unregistered operation became `requires_owner_decision`. Repeating\nboth scans found zero additional claims and did not duplicate uncertainty or\nwake state.\n\n## Exact-Head Validation\n\nExact head `2c69a09edeb0860d7885d23ac345bab770ee6bab` passed:\n\n- 100 durable tests: 92 in the cumulative durable shard and 8 in the\n  wake-dispatcher shard;\n- 9 plugin SDK surface-ratchet tests;\n- the three-connection settlement-fault, restart-recovery, no-replay, and\n  repeated-convergence trace above;\n- `pnpm tsgo:all`;\n- changed-file type-aware Oxlint;\n- `pnpm check:durable-canonical-naming`;\n- `pnpm lint:kysely` and `pnpm db:kysely:check`;\n- `pnpm lint:agent:ingress-owner`;\n- `pnpm deadcode:unused-files`;\n- Oxfmt and `git diff --check`;\n- `pnpm build`, reporting `OpenClaw 2026.7.1 (2c69a09)`.\n\nFull local evidence is recorded in\n`reports/openclaw-pr5-exact-head-operation-worker-proof-2026-07-19.md` in the\ncompanion analysis workspace.\n\n## Boundary\n\nThis PR does not claim exactly-once external effects. If a handler completes an\nexternal side effect before SQLite settlement fails, replay is permitted only\nwhen the owner explicitly supplies idempotency or equivalent safety. It does\nnot resume arbitrary operating-system processes, replay metadata-only agent\nturns, replace task/flow/subagent owners, add a schema, or expose public recovery\nmutation methods.\n\nPR6 remains the bounded read-only operational Gateway and CLI inspection\nsurface. It will not be submitted until this PR's latest completed overall\nClawSweeper rating reaches Gold Shrimp or higher.\n\nThis PR is AI-assisted. The implementation and proof were manually reviewed\nagainst operation/version isolation, transaction atomicity, attempt fencing,\nowner authority, no-replay, and convergence boundaries.\n",
